# The payTo check, against live data on both chains — 2026-09-07.
#
# ENS record on Sepolia vs the payTo in a live 402 from the demo provider.
# This is the one Verdikt check that must happen BEFORE the fact: a payment
# to a spoofed address never touches the bonded service, so there is nothing
# to reclaim it from.

## weather — ENS address matches the provider's payTo
$ curl -sD - http://localhost:8404/weather
HTTP/1.1 402 Payment Required
content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
x-verdikt-pay-to-verified: true

   relayed unchanged: the agent gets the provider's real challenge to sign.

## weather-lite — address record repointed to 0x…dEaD
$ curl -sD - http://localhost:8404/weather-lite
HTTP/1.1 502 Bad Gateway
x-verdikt-block: pay_to_mismatch

{
    "error": "pay_to_mismatch",
    "reason": "pay_to_mismatch",
    "detail": "challenge pays to 0x5c33f23555313256b71f2b0a7ea1938425516505, 0x5c33f23555313256b71f2b0a7ea1938425516505, 0x5c33f23555313256b71f2b0a7ea1938425516505, but the service published 0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD",
    "service": "weather-lite.verdikt.eth",
    "expectedPayTo": "0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD"
}

   blocked. The response carries no 'accepts', so no signable challenge
   reaches the agent — only prose naming both addresses for an operator.
